    objection: 'Doesn’t trusting Divine provision make people passive or lazy about working hard?',
    objectionReply:
      'Classical Islamic wisdom makes the exact opposite distinction: tie your camel first, then trust Allah. Ibn Ata Allah never counsels abandoning effort; he counsels abandoning inner panic while you work. A calm farmer plants better seeds than a frantic one.',
