    simpleContent:
      'Worry usually fills the heart not because there is not enough good in the world, but because we want to control the exact clock of our lives. Ibn Ata Allah pointed out how tired we get trying to force tomorrow to happen today.\n\nThere is a peaceful dividing line in life: your job is honest effort in the moment in front of you. God’s job is the timing and the outcome—the same Sustainer who cared for you before you could even walk or speak.\n\nNothing can rush what is not ready for you, and nobody can block what God has written for you. Dropping anxious control lets you work with a clear, steady heart.',
